id: gatt_client
package: bluetooth_le_siwx91x
description: >
  GATT Client event handlers for BLE
label: GATT Client
category: Device|Si91x|Wireless|BLE|GATT
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
component_root_path: ./components/device/silabs/si91x/wireless/gatt
provides:
  - name: gatt_client
define:
  - name: SL_SI91X_BLE_GATT_CLIENT_COMPONENT
source:
  - path: client/src/gatt_client_init.c
  - path: client/src/gatt_client_utilities.c
  - path: client/src/gatt_client_event_hdlrs.c

include:
  - path: client/inc
    file_list:
      - path: gatt_client.h

config_file:
  - path: client/inc/gatt_client_config.h
    directory: ble_config
    file_id: gatt_client_config

requires:
  - name: ble_unified_framework
  - name: gap
  - name: gatt_common

template_contribution:
  - name: ble_unified_config_includes
    value: "gatt_client_config.h"
  - name: ble_unified_init_hooks
    value:
      ble_unified_init_func: ble_gatt_client_init
      ble_unified_init_label: "GATT Client"
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_ext_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_INDICATE_CONFIRMATION_FROM_HOST
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_guard: RSI_BLE_INDICATE_CONFIRMATION_FROM_HOST
  - name: wrapper_implementations
    value:
      name: sl_btc_ble_gatt_client_register_callbacks_wrapper
      registration_api: rsi_ble_gatt_client_register_callbacks
      callbacks:
        - NULL
        - NULL
        - NULL
        - NULL
        - NULL
        - NULL
        - NULL
        - event_mtu
        - gatt_error_event
        - NULL
        - event_profiles_list
        - event_profile
        - event_char_services
        - NULL
        - NULL
        - on_read_resp_event
        - event_write_resp
        - NULL
  - name: ble_events
    value:
      event_mtu:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_mtu
            type: rsi_ble_event_mtu_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_mtu
      
      gatt_error_event:
        callback_params:
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
          - name: rsi_ble_event_error_resp
            type: rsi_ble_event_error_resp_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_error_resp
      
      event_gatt_desc:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_gatt_desc
            type: rsi_ble_event_gatt_desc_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_gatt_desc
      
      event_char_services:
        callback_params:
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
          - name: rsi_ble_event_read_by_type1
            type: rsi_ble_event_read_by_type1_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_read_by_type1
      
      event_profile:
        callback_params:
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
          - name: rsi_ble_event_profile_by_uuid
            type: rsi_ble_event_profile_by_uuid_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_profile_by_uuid
      
      event_profiles_list:
        callback_params:
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
          - name: rsi_ble_event_profiles_list
            type: rsi_ble_event_profiles_list_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_profiles_list
      
      event_write_resp:
        callback_params:
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
          - name: rsi_ble_set_att_resp
            type: rsi_ble_set_att_resp_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_set_att_resp
      
      prepare_write_resp:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_prepare_write_resp
            type: rsi_ble_prepare_write_resp_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_prepare_write_resp
      
      on_read_resp_event:
        callback_params:
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
          - name: rsi_ble_event_att_value
            type: rsi_ble_event_att_value_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_att_value
      
      event_on_data_receive:
        callback_params:
          - name: conn_id
            type: uint8_t
        event_data:
          name: conn_id
      
      event_data_transmit_client:
        callback_params:
          - name: conn_id
            type: uint8_t
        event_data:
          name: conn_id
      
      event_set_buffer_config_client:
        callback_params:
          - name: conn_id
            type: uint8_t*
        event_data:
          name: conn_id
                
      event_select_data_transfer:
        callback_params:
          - name: conn_id
            type: uint8_t*
        event_data:
          name: conn_id
      
      event_profile_discovery:
        callback_params:
          - name: conn_id
            type: uint8_t*
        event_data:
          name: conn_id
      
      event_profile_dummy:
        callback_params:
          - name: profile_dummy_data
            type: sli_profile_dummy_data_t*
        event_data:
          name: profile_dummy_data
  - name: agents_slab
    value:
      id: gatt_client
      context: |
        ## GATT Client Component (Si91x Wireless BLE Unified)
        Service/characteristic discovery and read/write operations against a remote GATT server. Selecting this component defines `SL_SI91X_BLE_GATT_CLIENT_COMPONENT` and brings in `gap` + `gatt_common` automatically.
        ### Init hook
        - Function: `ble_gatt_client_init` (registered via `ble_unified_init_hooks`).
        - Registers `sl_btc_ble_gatt_client_register_callbacks_wrapper()` covering: `event_mtu`, `gatt_error_event`, `event_profiles_list`, `event_profile`, `event_char_services`, `on_read_resp_event`, `event_write_resp` (and several internally-mapped slots that are NULL for this profile).
        ### Configuration (`gatt_client_config.h` — copied to `config/ble_config/`)
        Key macros: `PROFILE_QUERY_*` (which profiles to discover automatically post-connect), `DATA_TRANSFER_*` (notification/indication subscription flags), `RX_NOTIFICATIONS_FROM_*` and `RX_INDICATIONS_FROM_*` (per-peer subscriptions), client UUIDs to subscribe to. Optional bitmap contribution `SL_SI91X_BLE_INDICATE_CONFIRMATION_FROM_HOST` (gated by `RSI_BLE_INDICATE_CONFIRMATION_FROM_HOST`) — when set, the host explicitly sends indication confirmations instead of the controller doing so automatically.
        ### Discovery / Operation Order (CRITICAL)
        All GATT client operations require an active connection. Typical sequence after `event_enhance_conn_status` (status==success):
        1. `rsi_ble_get_profiles_async()` → completes in `event_profiles_list`.
        2. For each profile of interest: `rsi_ble_get_char_services_async()` → completes in `event_char_services`.
        3. (Optional) Subscribe to notifications: `rsi_ble_set_att_value_async()` writing 0x0001 to the CCCD (handle = char_value_handle + 1).
        4. Read/Write: `rsi_ble_get_att_value_async()` / `rsi_ble_set_att_value_async()` → complete in `on_read_resp_event` / `event_write_resp`. Errors arrive via `gatt_error_event`.
        ### Common Mistakes to Avoid
        - Issuing a GATT API before connection has fully established (wait for `event_enhance_conn_status`).
        - Pipelining multiple async GATT requests on the same connection — most paths assume one in-flight request per connection. Wait for the response/error event before issuing the next.
        - Computing CCCD handles by guesswork — always discover descriptors via `rsi_ble_get_att_descriptors_async()` (or pull them from the cached profile list) instead of assuming `value_handle + 1`.
        - Forgetting MTU exchange: notifications larger than the negotiated MTU-3 are silently truncated. After `event_mtu` reports the peer MTU, gate large writes/notify-payloads accordingly.
    priority: -5307
